.\\\" Man page for ccat-rs
.TH CCAT 1 "2026-06-21" "0.3.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ccat \\- The Terminal Swiss Army Knife \\- enhanced cat with 40+ features: file viewer, Linux system diagnostics, dev tools, and more
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ccat
[\\fI\\,OPTIONS\\/\\fR] [\\fI\\,FILES\\/\\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
ccat is an enhanced cat tool that automatically detects file types and renders them appropriately in the terminal. It also includes a comprehensive Linux system diagnostics suite, developer tools, charting engine, QR code generator, and more \\- all in a single Rust binary with zero runtime dependencies.

File viewing: Markdown rendering, Word document text extraction, image display (Kitty/Sixel/half-block), gzip transparent decompression, PDF text extraction, archive listing (zip/tar/deb/rpm), audio/video metadata, JSON/YAML/TOML/CSV formatting, log highlighting, ELF binary introspection, and diff viewing.

System diagnostics: unified health assessment with scoring (\\fB--health\\fR), memory analysis with bar charts (\\fB--meminfo\\fR), process list (\\fB--ps\\fR), CPU topology with AVX-512 flags (\\fB--cpu\\fR), disk/filesystem stats (\\fB--disk\\fR), network connections (\\fB--netstat\\fR), swap/ZRAM analysis (\\fB--swap\\fR), cgroup v2 hierarchy (\\fB--cgroup\\fR), OOM score analyzer (\\fB--oom\\fR), file descriptors (\\fB--fd\\fR), virtual memory maps (\\fB--vmmap\\fR), IRQ/SoftIRQ analysis (\\fB--interrupts\\fR), and scheduler analysis (\\fB--sched\\fR).

Developer tools: codebase TODO/FIXME scanner (\\fB--todo\\fR), regex search (\\fB--search\\fR), git object viewer (\\fB--git\\fR), file inspection with hashes (\\fB--inspect\\fR), schema inference (\\fB--schema\\fR).

Creative: QR code generation (\\fB--qr\\fR), ASCII charting (\\fB--chart\\fR), HTTP server (\\fB--serve\\fR), HTML output (\\fB--html\\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-diff\fR \fI<file1>\fR \fI<file2>\fR
Diff mode: compare two files.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-ascii\fR
Force plain text output (skip markdown/docx/image processing).
.TP
\fB\-B\fR, \fB\-\-binary\fR
Display raw bytes (no processing).
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-type\fR
Show detected file type (like the \fBfile\fR command).
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-number\fR
Number all output lines.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-number\-nonblank\fR
Number non-blank output lines.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-squeeze\-blank\fR
Squeeze consecutive blank lines into one.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-edit\fR \fI<expression>\fR
Apply sed\-like substitution (e.g. s/foo/bar/).
.TP
\fB\-\-completions\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Generate shell completions (bash, zsh, fish, etc.).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version.
.SH DETECTED FILE TYPES
ccat detects the following file types automatically:
.IP \[bu] 2
Markdown (.md, .markdown) \- rendered with syntax highlighting
.IP \[bu] 2
Word documents (.docx) \- text extraction with formatting
.IP \[bu] 2
Images (.png, .jpg, .gif, .webp, .bmp, .tiff) \- terminal display
.IP \[bu] 2
PDF (.pdf) \- text extraction
.IP \[bu] 2
Archives (.zip, .tar, .tgz, .bz2) \- file listing
.IP \[bu] 2
Audio/Video (.mp3, .flac, .ogg, .mp4, etc.) \- metadata display
.IP \[bu] 2
JSON (.json) \- formatted with syntax highlighting
.IP \[bu] 2
YAML (.yaml, .yml) \- syntax highlighting
.IP \[bu] 2
Log files (.log) \- level/timestamp highlighting
.IP \[bu] 2
Gzip (.gz) \- transparent decompression
.IP \[bu] 2
ELF binaries \- disassembly (x86/x86_64, three consecutive calls)
.SH BINARY VIEWER
When a binary file is detected, ccat displays its type and waits for a third consecutive invocation on the same file within 2 seconds to enter interactive hex dump or disassembly mode.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
Set to any non-empty value to disable colored output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Display a Markdown file with syntax highlighting:
ccat README.md
.TP
Show file types in a directory:
ccat -T src/
.TP
Compare two files:
ccat -D file1.txt file2.txt
.TP
Display line numbers:
ccat -n file.txt
.TP
Disassemble a binary (run three times):
ccat /bin/ls
.TP
View audio metadata:
ccat song.mp3
.TP
Extract PDF text:
ccat document.pdf
